// RotateWebhookSecretWithResponse Rotate the signing secret
//
// Mint a new signing secret for this webhook and return it ONCE in the
// response — it is never retrievable again, exactly like the secret from
// creation. The previous secret enters a 24-hour overlap window: during
// that window `X-Peppol-Signature-V2` carries one `v1=` signature per
// active secret (new first), so a receiver can accept either while it
// rolls out the new secret. The legacy `X-Peppol-Signature` switches to
// the new secret immediately. Rotating again before the window closes
// drops the older secret (max two active secrets).
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /v1/webhooks/{id}/rotate-secret (the `RotateWebhookSecret` operationId).
